    {
      "source": "aztec/statement_of_basis.pdf",
      "locator": "page 11, section: statement_of_basis",
      "exact_span": "Monitoring requirements for the Total Dissolved Solids (TDS) are established in the proposed permit because the discharge enters the Colorado River Basin, in accordance with the current Salinity policy and program outlined in the most current \"review, water quality standards for salinity, Colorado river system.\"",
      "affected_purpose": "B",
      "computation_change_reason": "Whether TDS/salinity monitoring is imposed because of basin entry and salinity policy affects which monitoring requirements are treated as applicable for FY2025."
    },
    {
      "source": "aztec/statement_of_basis.pdf",
      "locator": "page 11, section: statement_of_basis",
      "exact_span": "The objective of the policy is to achieve \"no salt return\" whenever practicable for industrial discharges and an incremental increase in salinity over the supply water for municipal dischargers.",
