      "computation_change_reason": "Identifies the operative salt-tonnage thresholds and the industrial-facility test pathway; different readings of facility type or which of the three tests applies would change limit/monitoring computations."
    },
    {
      "source": "aztec/statement_of_basis.pdf",
      "locator": "page 11, section: statement_of_basis",
      "exact_span": "TDS data obtained from the DMRs reveals that the discharge does not have a reasonable potential to exceed the 1 ton/day in salinity.",
      "affected_purpose": "A,B",
      "computation_change_reason": "Whether reasonable-potential findings relieve or modify enforceable salt limits versus serving only as narrative support affects which numeric comparisons and monitoring tiers apply."
    },
    {
      "source": "aztec/statement_of_basis.pdf",
      "locator": "page 11, section: statement_of_basis",
      "exact_span": "The highest monthly average Total Dissolved Solids reported during the last two years is 19 mg/l.",
      "affected_purpose": "A",
      "computation_change_reason": "This reported concentration feeds salt-load and waiver determinations; treating it as the governing compliance value versus an illustrative maximum would change calculated loads and limit comparisons."
    },
    {
      "source": "aztec/statement_of_basis.pdf",
      "locator": "page 11, section: statement_of_basis",
      "exact_span": "TDS = 19 mg/l * 8.34 lbs/gal * 0.177 MGD * 1 ton / 2000 lbs = 0.0140 tons/day",
      "affected_purpose": "A",
      "computation_change_reason": "The derived daily salt tonnage (0.0140 tons/day) is compared against the 1 ton/day threshold; different inputs, units, or flow assumptions in this calculation would change whether the facility is treated as under the limit."
    },
    {
      "source": "aztec/statement_of_basis.pdf",
      "locator": "page 11, section: statement_of_basis",
      "exact_span": "Since the TDS concentration is less than 500 mg/L, the discharge qualifies for a \"fresh water waiver\" irrespective of the total daily or annual or annual salt load.",
      "affected_purpose": "A,B,C",
      "computation_change_reason": "A fresh-water waiver may remove or alter enforceable numeric limit comparisons and monitoring obligations; interpreting waiver scope (concentration-only vs. load-based) changes A/B outcomes and how no-result or waived periods are classified under C."
